# Code Directory Boundary

- All application code must live under `code/`.
- Create package manifests, lockfiles, source code, tests, public assets, configs, generated types, build configs, and environment examples only inside `code/`.
- Run install, development, lint, typecheck, test, build, code generation, and framework commands with `code/` as the working directory.
- Never create `src/`, `app/`, `public/`, `tests/`, `package.json`, lockfiles, or framework configuration at the workspace root.
- Files outside `code/` are read-only except `.cursor/**`, which may be updated for rules, specs, task status, and test reports.
- Do not move, rename, overwrite, or delete the source Word document.
- Before editing or running a mutating command, confirm the target resolves inside `code/` or `.cursor/`.
- If a generator writes outside `code/`, stop, clean up only those generated files, and rerun it from `code/`.

